<title>UK: Saint-Gobain sells unit to Cookson.</title>
<headline>Saint-Gobain sells unit to Cookson.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>French glass maker Saint-Gobain said on Wednesday it was selling its subsidiary GRP Inc. to Britain's Cookson Group Plc for $45 million.  </p>
<p>Saint-Gobain said the sale was part of the condition put forward by the United States Federal Trade Commission (FTC).</p>
<p>In February 1996, the FTC authorised Saint-Gobain Industrial Ceramics to acquire Carborundum under the condition that three of its North American activities be sold or licensed.</p>
<p>GRP Inc., the former Monofrax division of Carborundum specialised in electrofused refactories for the glass industry, had to be sold by the end of February 1997.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
